WEBVTT

00:00.260 --> 00:04.496
The page's illustrative decision labels operational deliveries restricted.

00:04.496 --> 00:08.931
Approved Delivery Operations analysts may read necessary records to investigate

00:08.931 --> 00:11.134
performance, in a managed workspace.

00:11.134 --> 00:14.056
Does recording that purpose and classification establish

00:14.056 --> 00:16.583
that other accounts cannot retrieve the records?

00:16.583 --> 00:19.650
Pause and name the evidence needed to show that controls work.

00:24.523 --> 00:26.810
The label does not enforce access.

00:26.810 --> 00:31.705
Connect approval to identity groups, scoped database grants and catalogue visibility.

00:31.705 --> 00:33.803
Test permitted and restricted accounts through

00:33.803 --> 00:37.145
database access, search, APIs and exports.

00:37.145 --> 00:40.099
Team membership does not approve every purpose: an

00:40.099 --> 00:42.776
unrelated marketing analysis needs its own decision.

00:42.776 --> 00:46.708
Revoking a grant cannot retrieve an already downloaded spreadsheet, and technical

00:46.708 --> 00:48.810
access rarely proves why someone used it.

00:49.732 --> 00:55.500
Now consider the page's separate synthetic research dataset, version one point zero.

00:55.500 --> 00:58.511
Its identifier is pending, its public download is

00:58.511 --> 01:02.568
planned, and its proposed license is CC BY 4.0.

01:02.568 --> 01:04.109
No release has occurred.

01:04.109 --> 01:08.538
Does that planned publication authorise sharing the operational deliveries table?

01:08.538 --> 01:12.752
Explain which dataset and status each record concerns, then pause.

01:17.778 --> 01:18.368
No.

01:18.368 --> 01:22.824
The synthetic dataset contains invented parcels, not customer records.

01:22.824 --> 01:26.900
Its proposed license does not authorise exporting the operational table.

01:26.900 --> 01:30.943
FAIR means Findable, Accessible, Interoperable and Reusable.

01:30.943 --> 01:35.295
Documented retrieval, meaning, provenance and versions support reuse, but FAIR neither

01:35.295 --> 01:37.978
requires public access nor grants permission.

01:37.978 --> 01:42.327
A planned identifier and license do not establish a completed repository deposit.

01:43.375 --> 01:48.682
Protect the evidence itself: saved queries and samples may reveal individual details.

01:48.682 --> 01:50.915
Use parameters and synthetic samples where

01:50.915 --> 01:54.441
appropriate, and check indexes and exported copies too.

01:54.441 --> 01:57.784
Agree retention by artifact and purpose, including copies.

01:57.784 --> 02:02.836
Once the input snapshot is deleted, metadata may explain which input was used without

02:02.836 --> 02:04.451
enabling an exact rerun.

02:04.451 --> 02:07.654
A deletion record does not prove every unmanaged copy disappeared.

02:08.727 --> 02:10.959
Try the page's map exercise.

02:10.959 --> 02:14.010
In Access decision's Example record, distinguish

02:14.010 --> 02:16.712
approved purpose from evidence of enforced controls.

02:16.712 --> 02:18.635
Then open Reuse description.

02:18.635 --> 02:22.860
Compare its dataset version, pending identifier and proposed license with the

02:22.860 --> 02:24.588
operational access decision.

02:24.588 --> 02:27.244
Explain why these records do not authorise sharing

02:27.244 --> 02:30.355
operational rows, then use Check your answer.

02:30.355 --> 02:34.500
The page keeps the full controls, retention choices and publication requirements.
